sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch12-02> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch12-02--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch12-02--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on thompson1917-ch12-02: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.56" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.559"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.62"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Spiral versus non-spiral architecture can be scored from existing image libraries, including the radiolarian contrast Thompson draws. The causal step is harder: many shells grow by external addition without becoming logarithmic spirals, and many spirals arise by other routes, so a frequency difference would remain compatible with several growth rules. Available images support a comparative test on well-illustrated groups, not a direct measurement of incremental accretion." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Code shell coiling and growth mode for multilocular Foraminifera and for Radiolaria, then test whether exterior accretion predicts a higher frequency of logarithmic spirals. The tendency would be supported by a large excess of spirals among accretionary foraminifera after phylogenetic correction, and weakened if milioline and other accretionary tests are commonly non-spiral at rates similar to non-accretionary skeletons." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Exterior accretion is how most foraminiferal tests grow, so the proposed cause is partly built into the materials being compared.", "Coiling categories in taxonomic databases are coarse and phylogenetically clustered." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch12-02--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch12-02--grok--dataset-2>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch12-02--grok--dataset-3> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch12-02--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of thompson1917-ch12-02 by Grok 4.7: 0.55" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.55"^^xsd:double ;
